{"$schema":"https://json.schemastore.org/sarif-2.1.0.json","runs":[{"artifacts":[{"contents":{"text":"<scxml xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2005/07/scxml\"\n       xmlns:env=\"https://github.com/stateforward/scxml.rs/namespaces/env\"\n       version=\"1.0\" datamodel=\"ecmascript\" initial=\"s0\">\n  <datamodel>\n    <data id=\"key\"/>\n  </datamodel>\n  <state id=\"s0\">\n    <onentry>\n      <env:get name=\"API_TOKEN\" location=\"key\"/>\n    </onentry>\n    <transition target=\"done\"/>\n  </state>\n  <final id=\"done\"/>\n</scxml>\n"},"location":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml084-env-element.scxml"},"mimeType":"application/scxml+xml"}],"columnKind":"utf16CodeUnits","properties":{"diagnosticCounts":{"errors":1,"notes":0,"total":1,"warnings":0},"producer":{"kind":"validator"}},"results":[{"level":"error","locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml084-env-element.scxml"},"region":{"endColumn":15,"endLine":9,"startColumn":8,"startLine":9}}}],"message":{"markdown":"`<env:get>` is an element in the `env` namespace, which has none\n\n**Note:** `https://github.com/stateforward/scxml.rs/namespaces/env` is an attribute vocabulary only: an extension element's `env:<slot>=\"NAME\"` attribute names the variable whose value the host binds to that slot\n\n**Help:** remove the element, and put an `env:<slot>` attribute on the extension element that needs the value\n\n**Spec:** SCXML 1.0 §4.10 Extensibility of Executable Content","text":"`<env:get>` is an element in the `env` namespace, which has none"},"properties":{"byteSpan":{"end":276,"start":269},"category":"semantic"},"ruleId":"SCXML084"}],"tool":{"driver":{"informationUri":"https://www.w3.org/TR/scxml/","name":"scxml-validator","rules":[{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"`https://github.com/stateforward/scxml.rs/namespaces/env` is the host's attribute vocabulary for the slots of an executable-content extension element or an invoked service's `<invoke>`: it has no elements, an element in no namespace (inline data, for example) has no slots, and neither has the `<invoke>` of an SCXML session (an absent `type`, `scxml`, or `http://www.w3.org/TR/scxml/`). An `env` attribute on any other SCXML element is `SCXML068`"},"help":{"text":"How to fix: remove the element or attribute, and put an `env:<slot>` attribute on the extension element that needs the value.\n\nSpecification: SCXML 1.0 §4.10 Extensibility of Executable Content\n\nRun `scxml-cli --explain SCXML084` for examples."},"helpUri":"https://www.w3.org/TR/scxml/#extensibility","id":"SCXML084","name":"SCXML084","properties":{"category":"semantic"},"shortDescription":{"text":"the `env` namespace is used outside an extension element's or invoked service's attributes"}}],"semanticVersion":"0.2.0"}}}],"version":"2.1.0"}